<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.ingame.pub-parts-offload</string>
    <!-- HOURLY at minute :40 (no Hour key in StartCalendarInterval): move finished pub-corpus parts serv1 -> Mac,
         free them on serv1, then delete the serv1 temp_files/*.txt whose data is provably merged (owner 08.10.2026:
         serv1 keeps only the map ids; the data lives on the Mac and is moved as soon as a sweep ends).
         Source: scripts/ops/pub_parts_offload.sh (+ .py). Design: docs/SERVER_LAYOUT.md (pub-corpus row).
         Why a calendar minute and not StartInterval 3600: a fixed wall-clock phase (log lines always at :40, clear
         of the :00 cron-style jobs) that does not drift with load/wake time; like StartInterval, runs missed while
         the Mac sleeps are coalesced into one run on wake, and launchd never starts a second instance of a label that
         is still running (the script also holds a Mac-side lock).
         Hourly is safe because: the min-age option defaults to 1 h; an ssh/connect failure is only logged and notified once
         serv1 is unreachable for >6 h (reminder every 24 h); a repeated identical ABORT is notified once per 24 h; an
         unchanged temp_files leftover is not re-parsed; temp files are touched only when pub_recrawl.json says
         "complete" and no part file is left on serv1.
         Fail closed: any failed check aborts, nothing is deleted on serv1, the admin gets a Telegram
         message; exit 3 = skipped, retried next hour: a sweep holds serv1's pub_recrawl.lock, or a
         local dict build (explore_database.py / rebuild_dicts.sh / build_driver.py) reads the Mac corpus.
         TEMPLATE - NOT installed. Install: cp to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ and
         launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) <plist>  (re-install after editing: bootout, cp, bootstrap). Needs
         /bin/bash in Full Disk Access (TCC, as for the other ~/Documents jobs) and a non-interactive ssh key for
         `ssh serv1`. Read-only rehearsal: bash scripts/ops/pub_parts_offload.sh with the dry-run flag
         One-off run: launchctl kickstart gui/$(id -u)/com.ingame.pub-parts-offload
         Remove:      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.ingame.pub-parts-offload -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/alex/Documents/ingame/scripts/ops/pub_parts_offload.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>40</integer>
    </dict>
    <!-- No RunAtLoad: installing the job must not by itself start a transfer/delete. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/ingame_pub_parts_offload.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/ingame_pub_parts_offload.err</string>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/alex/Documents/ingame</string>
</dict>
</plist>
